<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61754" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λᾰκων-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <u>Laconian</u>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					628
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλειδίον</span>, a kind of
			key, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Th.</u>
				423
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aristopho
				7.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				343
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λακωνικὸν πνέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					276
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βραχυλογία τις Λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					343b
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλάττω ἔχειν γῆν τὸν ἀγρὸν
				ἐπιστολῆς Λακωνικῆς</span> Prov.in <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				1.2.30
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				38.5
			</span></i>. Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diph.
					96
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συντόμως καὶ Λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					13.52
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
				Subst., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Λακωνική</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>) <u>Laconia</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				245
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λακωνικαί</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμβάδες</span>), αἱ,
				<i>Laconian shoes</i>, used by men, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>V.</u>
				1158
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				142
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ec.</u>
				74
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				269
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -κόν</span>
			<i>the state of Lacedaemon</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.235
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ὁμιλίας τὸ Λ.</span>
			<u>Laconian</u> fashion, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cleom.</u>
				32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ Λ.</span>
			<i>Laconian steel</i>, St.Byz.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λακεδαίμων</span>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λακωνικόν, τό</span>, <i>female garment</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαφανῆ Λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Is.</u>
					3.23
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
